e  capital there were few signs that a  pandemic was on its way  which would consume our way of life  it has been a brutal year and from  westminster you can see it in microcosm  the infighting of brexit ending in the  finale in the house of commons but that  turned out to be a sideshow  in the face of the pandemic over here  saint thomas hospital  still inundated with coronavirus  patients  and it's where the prime minister had  his own close call with the virus  and on this side the london eye no  fireworks no spectacular  show it could be a symbol for cancelled  plans  and celebrations  but there is hope the vaccine rollout is  gathering steam  and in newcastle the faintest glint of  optimism  here fireworks were let off from secret  locations  so people wouldn't be tempted to gather  outside  it marks a new beginning and the end of  what has been  a terrible year alex rossi sky news
 

